<div class="bg-white min-h-screen">
  <!-- Navy hero: the millennial saint, received into the sanctuary -->
  <section class="relative bg-navy border-b-3 border-gold overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.05]" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/images/ornate-blue-gold-bg-symbols.jpg" alt="" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
    </div>
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-navy-dark/50 via-transparent to-navy-dark/70"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
    </div>

    <div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-14 md:py-20">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-10 md:gap-16 items-center">
        <figure class="relative mx-auto w-56 md:w-72 animate-rise">
          <div class="bg-halo absolute -inset-6 rounded-full animate-halo" aria-hidden="true">
          </div>
          <div class="relative bg-white p-2 pb-3 rounded shadow-ornate border-t-4 border-carlo">
            <img
              src="/images/carlo-acutis.jpg"
              alt="St. Carlo Acutis in his red polo shirt at Castelluccio"
              class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="relative font-garamond text-sm text-cream/70 text-center mt-3">
            Photo courtesy of the Associazione Amici di Carlo Acutis,
            <a
              href="https://www.carloacutis.com"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-gold-light hover:text-gold hover:underline"
            >
              carloacutis.com
            </a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="text-center md:text-left">
          <p
            class="inline-block font-cinzel text-xs md:text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gold-light border border-gold/45 bg-navy-dark/55 rounded-full px-5 py-2 mb-5 animate-rise"
            style="animation-delay: 100ms"
          >
            The First Millennial Saint
          </p>

          <h1
            class="font-cinzel text-4xl md:text-6xl text-cream mb-5 animate-rise"
            style="animation-delay: 180ms"
          >
            Saint Carlo Acutis
          </h1>

          <p
            class="font-garamond text-xl md:text-2xl text-gold-light italic max-w-xl leading-relaxed mb-8 animate-rise"
            style="animation-delay: 260ms"
          >
            A boy of daily Mass and the daily Rosary, who used the internet
            to point the world to heaven.
          </p>

          <div
            class="flex flex-wrap justify-center md:justify-start gap-x-8 gap-y-2 font-garamond text-base text-cream/75 animate-rise"
            style="animation-delay: 340ms"
          >
            <span>
              <span class="font-cinzel text-sm text-gold-light">1991&ndash;2006</span>
              London and Milan
            </span>
            <span>
              <span class="font-cinzel text-sm text-gold-light">Canonized</span>
              September 7, 2025
            </span>
            <span>
              <span class="font-cinzel text-sm text-gold-light">Feast</span> October 12
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- Jump strip -->
  <div class="border-b border-gold/25 bg-cream/60">
    <nav
      class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-3 flex flex-wrap justify-center md:justify-start gap-x-8 gap-y-2 font-cinzel text-xs tracking-[0.18em] uppercase"
      aria-label="On this page"
    >
      <a href="#life" class="text-gold-dark hover:text-gold transition-colors">His Life</a>
      <a href="#timeline" class="text-gold-dark hover:text-gold transition-colors">Timeline</a>
      <a href="#words" class="text-gold-dark hover:text-gold transition-colors">In His Words</a>
      <a href="#patron" class="text-gold-dark hover:text-gold transition-colors">
        Patron of Lumen Viae
      </a>
    </nav>
  </div>

<!-- His Life: magazine columns -->
  <section id="life" class="scroll-mt-8 py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[16rem_1fr] gap-8 md:gap-14 items-start">
        <div class="md:sticky md:top-8">
          <p class="font-cinzel text-xs tracking-[0.35em] uppercase text-gold-dark mb-3">
            An Ordinary Boy
          </p>
          <h2 class="font-cinzel text-navy text-3xl md:text-4xl leading-tight mb-4">
            An Extraordinary Love
          </h2>
          <div class="h-px w-16 bg-gold/40 mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="font-garamond text-brown-light italic leading-relaxed">
            Jeans, sneakers, soccer, video games&mdash;and the Blessed
            Sacrament at the center of everything.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="font-garamond text-brown text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed md:columns-2 md:gap-10 space-y-5">
          <p class="drop-cap">
            Carlo Acutis wore jeans and sneakers, loved soccer and video games,
            and taught himself to program. He held himself to one hour of video
            games a week, judging that anything more would come to own him.
            Nothing in his appearance set him apart from any other boy in Milan.
            What set him apart was invisible:
            from the day of his First Communion at the age of seven, he never
            willingly missed daily Mass, prayed the Rosary every day as his
            appointment with Our Lady, went to weekly confession, and stayed
            after Mass to keep company with Our Lord in the tabernacle.
          </p>
          <p>
            His faith was contagious. He led his own parents back to fervent
            practice, defended classmates who were bullied, spent his allowance
            on the poor of his neighborhood, and catechized the children of his
            parish. And he put his gift for computers at the service of the
            faith: at eleven he began an exhibition on the Eucharistic miracles
            of the world, which has since been received in thousands of parishes
            on five continents.
          </p>
          <p>
            When leukemia struck without warning in October 2006, he offered his
            sufferings for the Pope and for the Church, and died within days,
            at fifteen. He was beatified at Assisi in 2020 and canonized by
            Pope Leo XIV on September 7, 2025, the first saint of the
            millennial generation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="bg-parchment border-y border-gold/15">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-14 md:py-20">
      <.timeline moments={@moments} selected_moment={@selected_moment} />
    </div>
  </div>

<!-- In His Words: colophon quotes -->
  <section id="words" class="scroll-mt-8 py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="text-center mb-6">
        <p class="font-cinzel text-xs tracking-[0.35em] uppercase text-gold-dark mb-3">
          In His Words
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-cinzel text-navy text-4xl md:text-5xl">
          The Wisdom of a Fifteen-Year-Old Saint
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <.sacred_divider class="max-w-[210px] mx-auto" />
        <blockquote>
          <p class="font-garamond text-xl md:text-2xl text-navy italic leading-relaxed text-center">
            The Eucharist is my highway to heaven.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <.sacred_divider cross={false} class="max-w-[120px] mx-auto opacity-60" />
        <blockquote>
          <p class="font-garamond text-xl md:text-2xl text-navy italic leading-relaxed text-center">
            All people are born as originals, but many die as photocopies.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <.sacred_divider cross={false} class="max-w-[120px] mx-auto opacity-60" />
        <blockquote>
          <p class="font-garamond text-xl md:text-2xl text-navy italic leading-relaxed text-center">
            The Virgin Mary is the only woman in my life.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <.sacred_divider cross={false} class="max-w-[120px] mx-auto opacity-60" />
      </div>

      <p class="font-garamond text-lg text-brown-light italic text-center mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        And to his mother, in his last days: "Don't be afraid. Since Jesus
        became man, death has become the passage towards life."
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- Patron of Lumen Viae -->
  <div class="bg-parchment border-t border-gold/15">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-14 md:py-20">
      <section id="patron" class="scroll-mt-8">
        <div class="text-center mb-10">
          <p class="font-cinzel text-xs tracking-[0.35em] uppercase text-gold-dark mb-3">
            Why He Watches over This Work
          </p>
          <h2 class="font-cinzel text-navy text-4xl md:text-5xl">
            Patron of Lumen Viae
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="hairline-card p-6 md:p-8 hover:shadow-ornate hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-300">
            <p class="font-cinzel text-gold-dark text-sm tracking-[0.25em] mb-2" aria-hidden="true">
              I
            </p>
            <h3 class="font-cinzel text-navy text-2xl mb-3">He Prayed the Daily Rosary</h3>
            <p class="font-garamond text-brown text-lg leading-relaxed">
              Carlo kept a daily appointment with Our Lady on the beads. The
              devotion this site exists to serve was the fabric of his ordinary
              day, alongside Mass and adoration.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="hairline-card p-6 md:p-8 hover:shadow-ornate hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-300">
            <p class="font-cinzel text-gold-dark text-sm tracking-[0.25em] mb-2" aria-hidden="true">
              II
            </p>
            <h3 class="font-cinzel text-navy text-2xl mb-3">He Sanctified Technology</h3>
            <p class="font-garamond text-brown text-lg leading-relaxed">
              Carlo used websites and code to set the treasures of the faith
              before the world. Lumen Viae walks the road he opened: the
              meditations of the saints, carried by modern means to wherever
              you are.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="hairline-card p-6 md:p-8 hover:shadow-ornate hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-300">
            <p class="font-cinzel text-gold-dark text-sm tracking-[0.25em] mb-2" aria-hidden="true">
              III
            </p>
            <h3 class="font-cinzel text-navy text-2xl mb-3">He Proves It Is Possible</h3>
            <p class="font-garamond text-brown text-lg leading-relaxed">
              A boy who loved computers and video games became a canonized saint
              through the oldest means in the Church: the Eucharist, Our Lady, and
              fidelity in little things. He died before the first smartphone, and
              he already governed his screens rather than being governed by them.
              Sanctity is not out of reach.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto w-36 md:w-44 mt-12">
          <.carlo_icon />
        </div>
        <p class="text-center font-garamond text-xl text-navy italic mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          Sancte Carole Acutis, ora pro nobis.
        </p>
      </section>

<!-- Closing -->
      <div class="text-center mt-16">
        <.sacred_divider class="max-w-[210px] mx-auto" />

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center items-center mt-10">
          <.gold_cta navigate="/dashboard">
            Pray Today's Rosary
          </.gold_cta>
          <.link navigate="/true-devotion" class="btn-outline-gold text-navy">
            True Devotion to Mary
          </.link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
